In MOND, the actual acceleration \(a\) is related to the Newtonian acceleration \(a_N\) by \(a\,\mu(a/a_0)=a_N\) with \(\mu(x)=x/(1+x)\). For a homogeneous sphere of mass \(M\) and radius \(R_b\),

\[
a_N(r)=
\begin{cases}
\displaystyle\frac{GMr}{R_b^3}, & r\le R_b,\\[6pt]
\displaystyle\frac{GM}{r^2}, & r\ge R_b.
\end{cases}
\]

We consider two limiting regimes:

- **Newtonian regime (\(a\gg a_0\)):** \(\mu\approx1\) ⇒ \(a\approx a_N\).  
  Then \(v_c(r)=\sqrt{a_N r}\) gives
  \[
  v_c(r)=
  \begin{cases}
  \sqrt{\dfrac{GM}{R_b^3}}\, r, & r\le R_b,\\[6pt]
  \sqrt{\dfrac{GM}{r}}, & r\ge R_b.
  \end{cases}
  \]

- **Deep MOND regime (\(a\ll a_0\)):** \(\mu\approx a/a_0\) ⇒ \(a^2/a_0\approx a_N\) ⇒ \(a\approx\sqrt{a_0 a_N}\).  
  Then \(v_c(r)=\sqrt{a r}= (a_0 a_N)^{1/4} r^{1/2}\) gives
  \[
  v_c(r)=
  \begin{cases}
  \left(\dfrac{a_0 G M}{R_b^3}\right)^{\!1/4} r^{3/4}, & r\le R_b,\\[6pt]
  (a_0 G M)^{1/4}, & r\ge R_b.
  \end{cases}
  \]

For intermediate accelerations the full \(\mu\) function must be used, but the asymptotic forms above capture the essential behaviour.

\[
\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
\text{Newtonian: } & v_c(r)=\begin{cases}
\sqrt{\frac{GM}{R_b^3}}\, r, & r\le R_b,\\
\sqrt{\frac{GM}{r}}, & r\ge R_b;
\end{cases}\\
\text{Deep MOND: } & v_c(r)=\begin{cases}
\left(\frac{a_0 G M}{R_b^3}\right)^{1/4} r^{3/4}, & r\le R_b,\\
(a_0 G M)^{1/4}, & r\ge R_b.
\end{cases}
\end{aligned}}
\]
